RFC 3986 pct-encoded = "%" HEXDIG HEXDIG
the triplet check looks at the slice start only,
the encoding check looks at every '%' in the slice

a '%' at the slice start, followed by two hex digits:
  triplet("%20") = 1  (expected 1)  PASS
  triplet("%2F") = 1  (expected 1)  PASS
  triplet("%2f") = 1  (expected 1)  PASS
  triplet("%00") = 1  (expected 1)  PASS
  triplet("%FF") = 1  (expected 1)  PASS

not a well-formed triplet:
  triplet("%2") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS
  triplet("%zz") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS
  triplet("%2G") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS
  triplet("x20") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS
  triplet("") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS
  triplet("%") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS

whole slice: every '%' must open a well-formed triplet:
  encoding("a%20b") = 1  (expected 1)  PASS
  encoding("%00") = 1  (expected 1)  PASS
  encoding("%20%41") = 1  (expected 1)  PASS
  encoding("") = 1  (expected 1)  PASS
  encoding("abc") = 1  (expected 1)  PASS

malformed percent-encoding:
  encoding("a%b") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS
  encoding("%2") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS
  encoding("%zz") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS
  encoding("a%2") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS
  encoding("%%20") = 0  (expected 0)  PASS

PASSED
